<p>President Trump invoked Pearl Harbor while hosting Japanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi at the White House on March 19, after a Japanese reporter asked why Washington had not informed allies before striking Iran. Multiple reports said Trump replied that the U.S. had withheld advance notice because it wanted surprise, then added remarks referencing Japan and Pearl Harbor, drawing an awkward reaction from Takaichi in the Oval Office. The exchange came during an otherwise cordial first White House meeting between the two leaders. Both sides stressed the U.S.-Japan alliance, trade cooperation, regional security, and efforts tied to energy stability amid the Iran conflict. Trump praised Tokyo as &quot;really stepping up to the plate&quot; on Iran-related matters, while reports said he also pressed Japan to do more to support efforts to secure shipping through the Strait of Hormuz, highlighting both the alliance&#x27;s resilience and the strain created by the widening Middle East crisis.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Mth18qbHBMGVXUpYFUxiijSDFHo2wMu9YH-y_jzPdRp2DLCUQjHpOI9PW51_A7LbYnVMlzkp3qp64WPcsXtvTn6K6X4SCSfWdviRFSHfSNj4' alt='US President Donald Trump meets Japan’s Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi at the White House.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Domestic constraint: Semafor reported that Japanese public opinion overwhelmingly opposes the Iran war, adding to the pressure on Takaichi as U.S. military attention shifts away from Asia.</li><li>Alliance optics: The New York Times reported that Takaichi took a restrained, careful approach during her first White House visit and largely avoided the sharper public criticism Trump has aimed at some other allies.</li><li>Diplomatic test: SCMP reported that Takaichi was the first U.S. ally to meet Trump face to face amid concern that he might vent frustration at partners that had declined to help with the Iran effort.</li></ul><blockquote>We didn&#x27;t tell anybody about it because we wanted surprise. Who knows better about surprise than Japan? - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: He portrayed Japan as more responsive than some other partners, praising Tokyo over Iran-related efforts and contrasting it favorably with NATO during the Oval Office appearance. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983922/japan-pm-takaichi-placates-trump-on-iran-but-faces-pearl-harbor-surprise'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi: She told Trump that Japan opposed Iran&#x27;s nuclear programme and appealed to his desire to be seen as a peacemaker, while keeping her public reaction to the Pearl Harbor remark muted. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/japan-prime-minister-sanae-takaichi-meets-us-president-donald-trump-march-19-2026/article70763343.ece'>The Hindu</a>, <a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/20/world/asia/trump-japan-prime-minister-meeting.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Japanese government: Tokyo endorsed allied language on safe passage through the Strait of Hormuz but gave few details about what help Japan might actually provide, leaving its practical contribution unclear. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1983922/japan-pm-takaichi-placates-trump-on-iran-but-faces-pearl-harbor-surprise'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Semafor&#x27;s analysis: The outlet argued that Trump&#x27;s Middle East demands were testing even close Indo-Pacific alliances, despite the warm optics of Takaichi&#x27;s visit. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/19/2026/strain-evident-in-trump-takaichi-white-house-meeting'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-draws-parallel-between-pearl-harbor-and-us-strikes-on-iran-in-meeting-with-japanese-pm'>Trump draws parallel between Pearl Harbor and US strikes on Iran in meeting with Japanese PM</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/19/us/politics/trump-japan-pearl-harbor-oval-office-takaichi.html'>Trump Jokes About Pearl Harbor in Meeting With Japan’s Prime Minister</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/why-didnt-you-tell-about-pearl-harbor-trumps-quip-makes-japan-pm-awkward-11241054#publisher=newsstand'>&quot;Why Didn&#x27;t You Tell About Pearl Harbor?&quot; Trump&#x27;s Quip Makes Japan PM Awkward</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/19/trump-mocks-japan-pearl-harbor-iran-war'>Trump mocks Japan about Pearl Harbor in response to question about Iran war</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/19/2026/strain-evident-in-trump-takaichi-white-house-meeting'>Strain evident in Trump-Takaichi White House meeting</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-draws-parallel-between-pearl-harbor-and-us-strikes-on-iran-in-meeting-with-japanese-pm/article70763342.ece'>Trump draws parallel between Pearl Harbor and U.S. strikes on Iran in meeting with Japanese PM</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/us/diplomacy/article/3347220/trump-talks-japanese-prime-minister-sanae-takaichi-positive-start'>Trump compares Iran attack to Pearl Harbour in otherwise positive Takaichi talks</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/19/trump-jokes-about-pearl-harbor-in-front-of-japan-s-prime-minister-during-white-house-meeting'>Trump jokes about Pearl Harbor in front of Japan’s prime minister during White House meeting</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-why-didnt-you-tell-me-about-pearl-harbor-trump-says-when-japanese-reporter-asks-why-allies-didnt-know-about-iran-plan'>WATCH: &#x27;Why didn&#x27;t you tell me about Pearl Harbor?&#x27; Trump says when Japanese reporter asks why allies didn&#x27;t know about Iran plan</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-pearl-harbor-meeting-japanese-prime-minister/'>Trump brings up Pearl